### Session 6 lab: the Counter Desk prototype (reference solution).
### Seed data: Members 1 to 7. Only two copies start available (Status 'D'):
###   0099826704 copy 1 (The Firm) and 0099895102 copy 1 (Jurassic Park).
### MemberID 99 does not exist, which makes it a safe "unknown member" case.
### Check the Loan and BookCopy tables in SSMS after each step.

### ---- Checkpoint 1: read ----
GET http://localhost:3000/books
###
GET http://localhost:3000/books/0099826704
###
GET http://localhost:3000/books/0000000000

### ---- Checkpoint 2: add a book with its first copy (one transaction) ----

### 201: a Book row AND BookCopy number 1 (Status D)
POST http://localhost:3000/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isbn": "0000000010",
  "title": "Counter Desk Handbook",
  "yearPublish": "2026",
  "publisherId": 1,
  "bookCat": "NF",
  "authorId": 1,
  "rentalRate": 5.00
}

### 409: that ISBN is taken
POST http://localhost:3000/books
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isbn": "0000000010", "title": "Counter Desk Handbook", "yearPublish": "2026", "rentalRate": 5.00 }

### 400: rental rate under 2.50
POST http://localhost:3000/books
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isbn": "0000000011", "title": "Too Cheap", "yearPublish": "2026", "rentalRate": 1.00 }

### 400: publisher 99 does not exist. Nothing is left behind in Book or BookCopy.
POST http://localhost:3000/books
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isbn": "0000000012", "title": "Half Written", "yearPublish": "2026", "publisherId": 99, "rentalRate": 5.00 }

### ---- Checkpoint 3: search and add a copy ----
GET http://localhost:3000/books?title=sql
###
GET http://localhost:3000/books?bookCat=F&limit=3&page=2&sort=year&order=desc
###
POST http://localhost:3000/books/0000000010/copies
Content-Type: application/json

{ "copyNo": 2, "rentalRate": 5.50 }

### 409: copy 2 now exists
POST http://localhost:3000/books/0000000010/copies
Content-Type: application/json

{ "copyNo": 2, "rentalRate": 5.50 }

### 404: no such book
POST http://localhost:3000/books/0000000099/copies
Content-Type: application/json

{ "copyNo": 1, "rentalRate": 5.50 }

### ---- Checkpoint 4: rent and return ----

### 201: a Loan row appears (LoanNo comes back from the database), copy becomes M
POST http://localhost:3000/copies/rent
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isbn": "0099826704", "copyNo": 1, "memberId": 1 }

### 409: already rented
POST http://localhost:3000/copies/rent
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isbn": "0099826704", "copyNo": 1, "memberId": 2 }

### 404: no such member
POST http://localhost:3000/copies/rent
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isbn": "0099895102", "copyNo": 1, "memberId": 99 }

### 404: no such copy
POST http://localhost:3000/copies/rent
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isbn": "0099826704", "copyNo": 9, "memberId": 1 }

### 200: Loan.DateReturn is filled in, copy goes back to D
POST http://localhost:3000/copies/return
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isbn": "0099826704", "copyNo": 1 }

### 404: there is no open loan any more
POST http://localhost:3000/copies/return
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isbn": "0099826704", "copyNo": 1 }

### ---- Stretch ----

### Change a copy's rental rate (200)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/books/0000000010/copies/2
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rentalRate": 6.00 }

### How many copies are on the shelf? (200)
GET http://localhost:3000/books/0000000010/availability

### Delete a copy (204)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/books/0000000010/copies/2

### Bad JSON is caught by the error handler, not a stack trace (400)
POST http://localhost:3000/copies/return
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isbn": "0099826704",
